<title>USA: Sl Industries unaware of reason stock rose.</title>
<headline>Sl Industries unaware of reason stock rose.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNT LAUREL, N.J. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>SI Industries Inc said Tuesday it knows of no corporate developments to account for the rise in the price of its common stock for the day.</p>
<p>The company issued the statement in response to a request for a possible explanation from the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>SI Industries, a maker of power and data equipments and systems, announced on May 1 the sale of its SL Aubury subsidairy to Cooper Industries Inc. Terms of the sale were not disclosed.</p>
<p>SI Industries closed at 8-3/4, up 1-1/8, on the NYSE.</p>
